{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-108735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3x+6y.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=x+2y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3(x+2y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+2y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1) & =3z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=6z+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=6z+1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "42a8fe87162f76c05074b4543fc2775d4caf12ec4140192615aa1abdc3d74666"} {"question" "q-108735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2z+1"] ["math" "3z"] ["math" "3z+2"] ["math" "6z"] ["math" "6z+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6z+1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108750" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x+8y-1}{4}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=x+4y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108750" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2(x+4y)-1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+4y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1) & =\\frac{2z-1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=2z.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108750" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "42a8fe87162f76c05074b4543fc2775d4caf12ec4140192615aa1abdc3d74666"} {"question" "q-108750" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108750" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2z"] ["math" "3-2z"] ["math" "6-z"] ["math" "\\frac{2z-1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{z+2}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108750" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2z"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2{sin}^{2}⁡(3x+3y)-1.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(g(x,y))=-6x+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2{sin}^{2}⁡(3(x+y))-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =2{sin}^{2}⁡(3z)-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2{sin}^{2}⁡(3z).\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{csc}^{2}⁡(3z)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ \\int {csc}^{2}⁡(3z)\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3z) & =2x+K \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡(3z) & =-6x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-3K.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x+3y)=-6x+C\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\ng(x,y)=3x+3y.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "42a8fe87162f76c05074b4543fc2775d4caf12ec4140192615aa1abdc3d74666"} {"question" "q-108780" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108780" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3-{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}"] ["math" "3x+3y"] ["math" "3x+3y-1"] ["math" "x+y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108780" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x+3y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x-2y).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=6x+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2(x-y))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x-y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1-\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2z).\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2z)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3 \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2z)\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2z) & =3x+K \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2z) & =6x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2K.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-2y)=6x+C\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\ng(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-2y).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "42a8fe87162f76c05074b4543fc2775d4caf12ec4140192615aa1abdc3d74666"} {"question" "q-108849" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108849" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-2y)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x-2y)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2x-2y)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-2y)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-2y)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-108849" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-2y)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-149744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{10x+2y}{5x+y+1}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=5x+y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-149744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2(5x+y)}{(5x+y)+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=5x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=5+\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-5 & =\\frac{2z}{z+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{7z+5}{z+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=\\frac{7z+5}{z+1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-149744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "42a8fe87162f76c05074b4543fc2775d4caf12ec4140192615aa1abdc3d74666"} {"question" "q-149744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-149744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1-5z}{z+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{2z+1}{z+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{2z}{z+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{4z+5}{z+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{7z+5}{z+1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"} {"question" "q-149744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7z+5}{z+1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067912/state.json" "file_sha256" "398fd574b3f4f183af0c3daf598ac5683f40d0a010bd973004a4c1c2c4d8eb9b"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2265 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
